# Home Lab Server

Before starting, Fedora must be installed and there must be a user account that is in the sudoers group (e.g. %wheel on RHEL/Fedora systems).

## First Run

```
$ INITIAL=true ./run.sh
```

This runs a playbook that sets up public key authentication for a special Ansible user and disables password authentication entirely, which means this will command will work only once. You will be prompted for the SSH connection password and BECOME password for sudo privilege escalation.

## Subsequent Runs

```
$ ./run.sh
```

Runs the main server deployment playbook without prompting for any passwords.

